Suggests:
 qt6-image-formats-plugins,
 xdg-desktop-portal-gtk,
 wl-clipboard,
# SnipSnap ships /usr/bin/flameshot as a compatibility symlink, which a
# distribution's own flameshot package also owns, so the two genuinely cannot
# be co-installed -- say so rather than letting dpkg discover it as a file
# conflict. Provides keeps anything depending on the old name resolvable.
# These three lines are the only place this package still names another
# program, and they are load-bearing: dropping them lets an apt upgrade
# silently replace someone's flameshot, which is the trap the rename avoided.
Conflicts: flameshot
Replaces: flameshot
Provides: flameshot
Description: Take and annotate screenshots, on every monitor at once
 SnipSnap is a screenshot tool for Linux desktops. Select a region with the
 mouse, annotate it, then copy or save it.
 .
 On GNOME Wayland it installs a Shell extension that draws the selection
 overlay inside the compositor. That is what makes a selection spanning
 several monitors possible, and it is why the screen never flashes a portal
 permission dialog before every capture.
 .
 It has no update checker and no image-host uploader; nothing it does leaves
 the machine.
